  "name": "axial compression force-displacement curve",
  "definition": "axial compressive force (N, plotted as negative in the paper) vs axial displacement of the cranial vertebra (mm, compression positive here), last of 5 tension-compression cycles (+200/-1000 N) at 5 mm/min; value = midline of the narrow experimental hysteresis loop",
  "unit": "N"
 },
 "source": {
  "short": "Marini 2016",
  "authors": "Marini G, Studer H, Huber G, Püschel K, Ferguson SJ",
  "year": 2016,
  "journal": "Biomech Model Mechanobiol 15:543-560",
  "doi": "10.1007/s10237-015-0709-6",
  "n": 6,
  "sample": "6 human lumbar intervertebral discs with their vertebral bodies (2 L2-L3, 4 L4-L5), posterior vertebral arches and soft tissues removed; experiments of Marini et al. 2015; Thompson grade 1-3",
  "age": "34, 34, 35, 35, 39, 47 y (specimens 1-6)",
  "sex": "not reported",
  "height_cm": null,
  "weight_kg": null
 },
 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Isolated disc-vertebra units vertically aligned in a dynamic materials testing machine; caudal vertebra fixed on a transverse sliding table; axial displacement applied to the cranial vertebra at constant rate 5 mm/min (quasi-static) between +200 N tension and -1000 N compression, 5 cycles; last cycle (offset from preconditioning removed) reported (Fig 9). No preload.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model the disc with its two vertebral bodies, posterior elements removed (specimen geometry: Table 3 volume and endplate area)",
   "Fix the caudal vertebra (allow transverse sliding); load the cranial vertebra axially",
   "Apply axial compression slowly (5 mm/min) from zero load up to 1000 N",
   "Report the compressive force at each axial displacement (0.1 mm steps) and compare with the specimen curve"
  ],
  "subject_model": null,
  "notes": "Primary experiments are Marini et al. 2015 (not in the repository); the curves are taken from the experiment lines of Fig 9 in Marini 2016 (the FE predictions are the dotted lines and were not extracted). Displacement zero = zero-force point of the loop."
 },
